Purpose: Make native machine cameras discoverable without typing a numeric source into a masked URL field.

Tasks:
  [x] Add local-camera versus custom URL/file/index source modes.
  [x] List Windows device names asynchronously without opening capture streams.
  [x] Preserve the selected camera's matching backend/index pair.
  [x] Keep source switching, environment URLs, presets and session lifecycle consistent.
  [x] Verify routing/failure paths, update tutorial/docs/context, and commit this workstream.

Acceptance criteria:
  Selecting a named device passes its actual index and capture API to the existing pipeline.
  Metadata discovery never calls VideoCapture or reads frames.
  Phone URLs and video files remain available; switching modes does not lose the entered URL.
  No camera starts merely from opening the studio, refreshing, or selecting a device.
  Discovery errors and empty results remain explicit; manual index input still works.

Completion evidence:
  Full suite: 236 passed; Ruff passed. Async discovery and mode switching covered.
  Actual Windows metadata returned Integrated Camera under MSMF and DirectShow, plus OBS Virtual Camera.
  No camera streams were opened; hardware frame capture remains the user's explicit Start action.
  README, tutorial, architecture and native-selector screenshot updated.
  Handbook rendered with zero diagram failures and zero overflowing pages.
